find asymptotic emulators of rules as well as the density of nonzero sites.
   All rules discussed in this paper were either class 1 or class 2 according
to Wolfram’s classification. Sequences of preimage numbers for chaotic
rules (except surjective rules) appear to be much more complex, and
no patterns seem to appear. If any regularities exist, their detection will
most certainly require computation of many more terms of the sequence,
and a more efficient algorithm may be necessary. P. Grassberger pro-
posed such an algorithm in [1], but even with his method going beyond
n ! 20 becomes impractical. Another method proposed in [2], called
the statistical inverse iteration, is unfortunately only approximate, thus
not very usable for the purpose of exact enumeration.

